# Backend testing (required)

**Every new/changed backend behavior must have tests.** CI gate: **100% coverage on `src/`** (`fail_under = 100` in `pyproject.toml`).

## When to add tests

| Change | Required tests |
|--------|----------------|
| New use case | Unit test with fake repositories; all guard branches + happy path |
| Domain aggregate/VO logic | Unit test in `tests/domain/` |
| New/changed repository method | Integration test with `db_session` fixture (SQLite in-memory) |
| New route | API test with `dependency_overrides` + assert status/body/cookies |
| New exception type | Assert status code in exception handler test |
| Mapper change | Round-trip test domain ↔ model |

## Structure

Mirror `src/` under `backend/tests/`:

```
tests/domain/
tests/application/
tests/infrastructure/
tests/interfaces/
tests/conftest.py   ← fakes, factories, db_session
```

## Patterns

- **Use cases**: `FakeUserRepository`, `FakeMealPlanRepository` from `conftest.py`; mock LLM via `@patch("...generate_meal_plan")`.
- **Repositories**: use `db_session` fixture; for expiry checks use `sqlite_utc_now` fixture (naive datetimes).
- **Routes**: override FastAPI deps on `app.dependency_overrides`; use `TestClient` or `httpx.AsyncClient`.
- **Exception handler**: call handler directly with each `EXCEPTION_STATUS_MAP` entry.
- Tests omit pydocstrings (`D` ignored for `tests/**`).

## Commands

```bash
cd backend
make test          # pytest
make test-cov      # pytest + 100% coverage gate
make check         # ruff + mypy
```

## Definition of done (backend)

- [ ] Tests added/updated for all new branches
- [ ] `make test-cov` passes (100%)
- [ ] `make check` passes
- [ ] No unrelated files changed
